🎯 DevSecOps Interview Series – Q1

Q: What is DevOps, and how is DevSecOps different? Give a real-time example ?

🔹 DevOps is all about collaboration and automation between development and operations teams. It speeds up software delivery through CI/CD pipelines.
🔹 DevSecOps takes DevOps further by embedding security into every stage of the pipeline. 
 It ensures that speed doesn’t compromise safety.
 
💡 Real-Time Example:

 In a Kubernetes CI/CD pipeline:

• DevOps deploys fast: code → build → test → deploy.
• DevSecOps deploys fast and runs security checks:
• ✅ SAST during build
• ✅ Container image scanning
• ✅ Secrets management
• ✅ Policy checks before deployment
This way, vulnerabilities are caught early—before they reach production
